---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Material Density Reference | SteelCalc" description="Planning reference for nominal steel, cement, concrete, sand, aggregate, and water densities used in quantity estimation.">
  <div class="page"><header><a href="/" class="brand">Steel<span>Calc</span></a><nav><a href="/calculators">Calculators</a><a class="active" href="/guides">Guides</a><a href="/tools">Tools</a></nav></header>
    <main><div class="eyebrow">MATERIAL REFERENCE</div><h1>Nominal densities for <em>estimating.</em></h1><p class="intro">These values are convenient planning references, not laboratory measurements. Replace them with project or supplier-specific data when accuracy matters.</p>
      <div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Material</th><th>Reference density</th><th>Typical use in SteelCalc</th><th>Qualifier</th></tr></thead><tbody>
        <tr><td>Steel</td><td>7,850 kg/m³</td><td>Steel section and plate weight</td><td>Nominal solid-steel density</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Cement (bulk)</td><td>1,440 kg/m³</td><td>Cement-bag estimating</td><td>Bulk density assumption; varies by packing</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Concrete</td><td>2,400 kg/m³</td><td>General reference only</td><td>Mix and aggregate change density</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Water</td><td>1,000 kg/m³</td><td>Volume-to-mass reference</td><td>Approximate near room temperature</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Sand</td><td>1,600 kg/m³</td><td>General planning reference</td><td>Loose density varies with moisture and grading</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Aggregate</td><td>1,500 kg/m³</td><td>General planning reference</td><td>Bulk density varies by size and packing</td></tr>
      </tbody></table></div>
    </main>
  </div>
</Layout>
<style>
:global(body){margin:0;background:#f6f7f8;color:#17212b;font-family:Inter,ui-sans-serif,system-ui}.page{max-width:1120px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 28px 70px}header{height:78px;border-bottom:1px solid #e1e6e9;display:flex;align-items:center}.brand{font-size:18px;font-weight:850;text-decoration:none;color:#17212b;margin-right:auto}.brand span{font-weight:450;color:#6c7780}nav{display:flex;gap:24px}nav a{font-size:10px;font-weight:700;color:#68747d;text-decoration:none}.active{color:#17212b}main{padding-top:55px}.eyebrow{font-size:7px;letter-spacing:1.8px;font-weight:850;color:#8b959d}h1{font-size:clamp(42px,5vw,64px);line-height:1;letter-spacing:-3.4px;margin:16px 0}h1 em{font-family:Georgia,serif;font-weight:500;color:#d9932f}.intro{max-width:760px;font-size:10px;line-height:1.8;color:#66747d}.table-wrap{overflow:auto;margin-top:32px}table{width:100%;min-width:760px;border-collapse:collapse;background:#fff;border:1px solid #e0e5e8}th,td{text-align:left;padding:13px 14px;border-bottom:1px solid #edf0f2;font-size:9px;line-height:1.65}th{font-size:7px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:1px;color:#87929a;background:#fafbfb}td:first-child{font-weight:800;color:#38454d}
</style>